nodes.prompt:
Brand: {{brand.brand_name}} — {{brand.brand_summary}}
Voice: {{brand.voice_tone}}
Value props: {{brand.value_props}}
Audience: {{brand.target_personas}}

Why it exists: {{inputs.why}}
The proof: {{inputs.proof}}
CTA: {{inputs.cta}}
Casting note: {{inputs.presenter}}

Cast the founder and write 3 beats to camera: beat 1 is the reason this exists, beat 2 is the proof they mean it, beat 3 is the invitation.

`actor` must pin identity down hard enough to repeat: apparent age, build, hair, face details, exact workwear including colour and fabric, and the specific working space with named objects in it.

`master_frame_prompt` is a still-image prompt for the opening frame of this person standing in that space, looking into the lens. Describe the person, their workwear, the room and the light — no camera brand names, no quality adjectives, no text.

For each of the 3 shots write:
- `frame_prompt`: an EDIT instruction on the master frame. Always start with "Same person, same hair, same clothes, same room, still looking into the lens." then change only expression, posture and how much of the room is visible. Beat 2 may come closer; beat 3 should open out and soften.
- `motion_prompt`: what happens in the 8 seconds AFTER that frame — delivery only. Include the spoken line in double quotes.
- `line`: just the spoken words, at most 18 words so it fits in 8 seconds.

`on_screen_text`: one caption per beat, at most 5 words each.
